# Develop AI-agentic strategic design practices to augment complex CX work and build team capability

## Purpose

Share after the exploration, as the formal development goal.

## Goal statement

This FY, I will develop and test AI-agentic ways of working that strengthen my practice as a strategic design and CX systems practitioner, while supporting our team goal to continue growing our capability as a Strategy and Design Team through learning, experimentation and fun.

My work often involves complex, ambiguous problems across customer strategy, channel experience, CRM adoption, information architecture, knowledge management, customer data, governance, stakeholder alignment and delivery planning. These areas are connected, but they are often managed through separate tools, artefacts and conversations.

I want to use AI agents responsibly to help me augment this work — not by replacing judgement, but by improving how I frame problems, synthesise information, test options, identify blind spots, avoid unproductive rabbit holes, separate evidence from assumptions, create reusable artefacts and communicate decision logic.

A key development focus will be improving how I bring people along the journey. I want to use AI-agentic practices to help me make complex work easier for others to understand, compare options more clearly, explain the rationale behind recommendations, surface assumptions earlier and create artefacts that support stronger stakeholder alignment.

I will apply this through live CX work such as Channel Strategy Year 2, information architecture, customer account management, knowledge management and CX strategy tools. I will also help translate what I learn into Team Goal 6 activities, including hack-a-thons, prototyping sessions, team learning activities and reusable practice resources.

By the end of the FY, I aim to have developed a practical, repeatable approach for AI-augmented strategic design work that improves my own effectiveness and helps the team build confidence in using AI to support strategy, design and customer experience work.
